    "notes": "<p data-pm-slice=\"0 0 []\"><strong>Cpt. Olga Kramarenko</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Occupation:</strong> MSS Agent<br><strong>Age:</strong> 36<br><strong>Personality:</strong> Direct</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>ATTRIBUTES</strong></h3>\n<p><strong>STRENGTH:</strong> 5<br><strong>WITS:</strong> 3<br><strong>EMPATHY:</strong> 3<br><strong>AGILITY:</strong> 3</p>\n<p><strong>HEALTH:</strong> 5</p>\n<hr>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>SKILLS</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Close Combat:</strong> 3</li>\n<li><strong>Ranged Combat:</strong> 3</li>\n<li><strong>Command:</strong> 4</li>\n<li><strong>Observation:</strong> 2</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>TALENTS</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pull Rank</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Buddy:</strong> To be chosen in the final act.<br><strong>Rival:</strong> Qiang</p>\n<p><strong>Signature Item:</strong> Bravery Medal</p>\n<hr>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>EQUIPMENT</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>UPP 9mm Service Pistol</strong> (2 loads)</li>\n<li><strong>Large Serrated Underwater Combat Knife</strong> (DMG 2)</li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: bold;\"><strong>P-DAT</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>Backstory</strong></h3>\n<p>Cpt. Olga Kramarenko once commanded an elite unit of underwater demolition commandos. Her unshakable loyalty to the UPP was severely tested about a year ago when her entire team was abandoned in enemy-infested waters. She emerged as the sole survivor.</p>\n<p>Awarded a bravery medal for her actions, Olga found herself emboldened enough to question her superiors about the decisions that led to this military catastrophe. Their response was swift: she was \"promoted\" and reassigned to the <strong>Ministry of Space Security</strong>, ostensibly as a reward for her valor, but in reality, it was a means of sidelining her.</p>\n<p>Her next assignment took her to the aquatic world of <strong>Voda</strong>, tasked with investigating a series of disappearances. Cautious but dutiful, Olga prepared for the mission, knowing full well she couldn't trust the motives of her superiors.</p>\n<p>She was warned about the station&rsquo;s <strong>chief engineer, Cixin Liu</strong>, whose repeated incompetence had compounded the station's troubles.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "adhocitems": ""
  },
